TECHO5 Checkers builds on the work of other open-source projects.

TECHO5, https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5 (MIT)
  The echod daemon, the Linux image tooling and the rootfs slot design this port reuses and adapts.

amonet, https://github.com/R0rt1z2/amonet (mt8163-checkers branch)
  The bootROM + LK bootloader exploit this device's unlock is built on — the same author's
  mt8163-cronos branch is what TECHO5 itself (the 2nd-gen Show 5) is built on.

Empty2k12, https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5/pull/2
  The hardware research in docs/hardware.md — how checkers differs from the 2nd-gen Show 5, read
  from the kernel source — comes from their checkers write-up in that pull request.
